 "script": {
  "hook": "Every team logs events. So why is half the data unusable?",
  "question": "Design an analytics event schema and naming.",
  "trap": "The trap: log whatever each screen wants. Names drift, types change, and nobody can query it.",
  "steps": [
   "Naming rule. Use object then action, in past tense, like message sent.",
   "Envelope. Every event carries the same fields: name, id, time, user, session, and version.",
   "Typed properties. Each event has a typed contract. Use enums, not free text. No personal data.",
   "Registry. Keep a tracking plan in code. Generate event types, and fail the build on unknown events."
  ],
  "takeaway": "One naming rule, one envelope, one registry.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: batching and flushing events.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
